# University Backend Rules

## Sequelize Multi-Tenancy (strict explicit mode)

Use explicit-only tenant scoping.

### Allowed DB access

Only use:

scoped(model).findAll()
scoped(model).findOne()
scoped(model).findByPk()
scoped(model).findAndCountAll()
scoped(model).count()
scoped(model).create()
scoped(model).bulkCreate()
scoped(model).update()
scoped(model).destroy()

Never call model methods directly.

Forbidden:

* model.findAll()
* model.findOne()
* model.findByPk()
* model.findAndCountAll()
* model.count()
* model.create()
* model.bulkCreate()
* model.update()
* model.destroy()
* applyMultiTenancy()
* monkey patching Sequelize
* overriding model methods

---

## Scope Behavior

Preserve existing buildScope() behavior.

Must continue supporting:

* university scope
* institute scope
* academic year scope
* teacher restriction
* AsyncLocalStorage requestContext
* bypass mode

Tenant values:

* come only from buildScope(model)
* never from request input
* never default manually from requestContext.getStore()

---

## WHERE Merge Rule (mandatory)

Tenant scope must always win.

Use:

where: {
...(options.where || {}),
...baseWhere
}

Never:

where: {
...baseWhere,
...options.where
}

Apply everywhere:

* root queries
* includes
* updates
* deletes
* counts

---

## Create / BulkCreate

Inject tenant values automatically from buildScope().

Before injection:

* filter scope keys using model.rawAttributes
* ignore missing tenant fields silently

Example:

Model:
{
title
}

Scope:
{
instituteId: 1
}

Insert:
{
title: "Math"
}

Model:
{
title,
instituteId
}

Insert:
{
title: "Math",
instituteId: 1
}

Tenant values always override payload values.

---

## Tenant Isolation

Strict isolation:

* read → scoped
* update → scoped
* delete → scoped
* create → injected tenant fields
* bulkCreate → same behavior

If record cannot be fetched due to scope:

* never update
* never delete
* never modify outside scope

Cross-tenant access must never be possible.

---

## Repository Style

Keep changes minimal.

Prefer:

* inline where/include
* existing architecture
* modifying existing functions

Avoid:

* helper explosion
* extra abstractions
* deep nesting
* unnecessary constants
* rewriting files

Repository owns business queries.

Service:

* thin pass-through

Controller:

* controller → service/repository only

---

## Query Pattern

Prefer:

const { rows: result, count: totalCount } =
await scoped(model.example).findAndCountAll({
where: {
...(id && { id })
},
include: [{
model: model.related,
where: {
...buildScope(model.related)
},
required: true
}],
offset: (page - 1) * limit,
limit,
distinct: true
});

return {
result,
totalCount,
page,
limit,
totalPages: Math.ceil(totalCount / limit)
};

List APIs return:

{
result,
totalCount,
page,
limit,
totalPages
}

---

## Routes

* validate() with Zod for write/list filters
* keep REST resource paths distinct
* update Postman collection when APIs change
